  "title": "Chapter 44: Agriculture in India",
  "order": 44,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z8t0c4u",
      "content": "Agriculture is the backbone of the Indian economy. A large portion of India's population depends on agriculture for livelihood. Agriculture not only provides food for the population but also supplies raw materials to many industries such as textiles, sugar and food processing."
    },
