      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Problems of Indian Agriculture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fvzvcwm",
      "content": "• Small land holdings."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yz33u5o",
      "content": "• Dependence on monsoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fj7cl1g",
      "content": "• Low productivity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oq2q3d6",
      "content": "• Lack of modern technology."
    },
    {
      "id": "9pwc9hg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Government Initiatives"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Dr. M.S. Swaminathan is recognized as the Father of the Green Revolution in India, whereas Dr. Norman Borlaug led the movement globally.",
        "PM-KISAN provides direct financial support of ₹6,000 per year to eligible landholding farmer families in three equal installments.",
        "Rice is India's primary staple crop, requiring high temperature (above 25°C), high humidity, and annual rainfall exceeding 100 cm.",
        "Operation Flood (White Revolution) was launched in 1970 under the leadership of Dr. Verghese Kurien to transform India into a milk-sufficient nation."
      ],
      "id": "oxit1di"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5zr9dem",
      "content": "• Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana – crop insurance scheme."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "daclgfu",
      "content": "• Soil Health Card Scheme – improves soil fertility."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rqgct35",
      "content": "• Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana – irrigation development."
    },
    {
